### Order Service — HTTP scenarios (dev)
### Base URL: http://localhost:8081
### All customer-facing endpoints require a Keycloak JWT (realm role "user").
### Owner console order list requires realm role "owner".
### Payment webhook (/api/payments/**) is open but requires no JWT (stub).
### Run top-to-bottom: each request depends on variables set by the previous one.
###
### Prerequisites:
###   • Keycloak on :8180 (realm keepdishesgoing), a user with realm role "user" (and one with "owner")
###   • order-service on :8081, restaurant-service on :8080
###   • Replace @restaurantId and @menuItemId below with REAL IDs from restaurant-service.

### Variables
@baseUrl    = http://localhost:8081
@keycloak   = http://localhost:8180
@restaurantId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@menuItemId  = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### 0. Acquire a customer access token (password grant — realm role "user")
# @name customerToken
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/keepdishesgoing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=restaurant-service&client_secret=upJ1DRbuRkHL3RKxRy0ib0ZJ4mkNIjWS&username=customer&password=customer

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

### 0b. (Optional) Owner access token for the order-list endpoint (realm role "owner")
# @name ownerToken
POST {{keycloak}}/realms/keepdishesgoing/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=restaurant-service&client_secret=upJ1DRbuRkHL3RKxRy0ib0ZJ4mkNIjWS&username=owner&password=owner

> {%
    client.global.set("ownerToken", response.body.access_token);
%}

### 1. Create cart (owner = JWT subject; no customerId in body)
# @name createCart
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/carts
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("cartId", response.body.cartId);
    client.log("cartId = " + response.body.cartId);
%}

### 2. Add item to cart (US15 / US16 — first add pins the restaurant)
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "menuItemId":   "{{menuItemId}}",
  "itemName":     "Margherita",
  "quantity":     2,
  "unitPrice":    10.50,
  "restaurantId": "{{restaurantId}}"
}

### 3. Get cart snapshot (review before checkout, US15)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4. Update item quantity
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/carts/{{cartId}}/items/{{menuItemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 3 }

### 5. List menu via proxy (US39 — symbol resolved from restaurant type)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/restaurants/{{restaurantId}}/price-category
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 6. Checkout (US17 / US18 / US19 / US20) — customerId comes from JWT
# @name checkout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cartId":       "{{cartId}}",
  "customerName": "Ruben",
  "street":       "Langestraat",
  "number":       "12",
  "postalCode":   "2000",
  "city":         "Antwerpen",
  "country":      "BE",
  "email":        "ruben@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("orderId", response.body.orderId);
    client.global.set("paymentRef", response.body.paymentRef);
    client.log("orderId = " + response.body.orderId);
    client.log("paymentRef = " + response.body.paymentRef);
%}

### 7. Confirm payment (stub webhook — permitAll but requires shared-secret header)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentRef}}/status
X-Payment-Signature: dev-secret-change-me

### 8. Place order (US18 freeze; publishes order.placed)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "PLACED" }

### 9. Tracking (US21 — current status + history)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/tracking
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 10. Get order detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 11. Cancel (only valid until ACCEPTED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CANCELLED", "reason": "customer changed mind" }

### 12. Customer order history (self, derived from JWT subject)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/customer
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 13. Owner order list (role owner)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/restaurant/{{restaurantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}


